592186245691 1145 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=5{x}^{2}+4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5{x}^{2}+4}\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1} & ={\\frac{10x}{5{x}^{2}+4}|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(1)}{5({1}^{2})+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245693 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245694 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1041 "field-1" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245693 13194139533671 true] [17592186245692 1110 #uuid "422c0e8e-ef2d-54e8-8efc-86f338261860" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245693 1034 "\\frac{10}{9}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245693 1111 #uuid "0cefcefd-ab4a-54a9-96ec-7fd9e98ed060" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245694 1034 "\\frac{5}{9}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245694 1111 #uuid "58f78de1-bf51-5725-9729-7397ef887e04" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245696 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1089 "q-310145" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={log}_{4}⁡(6x-2)+7$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1113 #uuid "cf7bff88-8076-590c-9d6c-accf8b15a565" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1138 false 13194139533671 true] [17592186245695 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{4}⁡(u)+7,\\,u=6x-2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(4)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(4)}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(6x-2)ln⁡(4)}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{(6x-2)ln⁡(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(3x-1)ln⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1} & =\\frac{3}{(3x-1)ln⁡(4)}{|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{(3(1)-1)ln⁡(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2ln⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245696 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245697 13194139533671 true] [17592186245696 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533671 true] [17592186245696 1041 "field-1" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245696 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245697 13194139533671 true] [17592186245696 1110 #uuid "fedb2062-2878-5cb4-970d-33e6a45be825" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245697 1034 "\\frac{3}{2\\ln(4)}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245697 1111 #uuid "a389446e-6169-5e82-8df7-14b55703d5ce" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245699 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1089 "q-341671" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1100 "Given that $f(x)=ln⁡(9x)$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1113 #uuid "06e078d9-14de-5fbb-a951-fa0bc181f2a8" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1138 false 13194139533671 true] [17592186245698 1145 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=9x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=9.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9x}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{9}}{\\cancel{9}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245699 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245700 13194139533671 true] [17592186245699 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533671 true] [17592186245699 1041 "field-1" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245699 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245700 13194139533671 true] [17592186245699 1110 #uuid "63ce6489-6b9c-5c3e-8c95-d580615b8b68" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245700 1034 "\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245700 1111 #uuid "76e7711b-030e-5e3e-bceb-b26a6febfd28" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245702 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1089 "q-341679" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=ln⁡(7-4x)$ at the point where $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1113 #uuid "0bdbe537-8874-525b-aec8-402f441a2044" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1138 false 13194139533671 true] [17592186245701 1145 "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=ln⁡u,\\,u=7-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-4x}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=-1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=-1} & ={-\\frac{4}{7-4x}|}_{x=-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7-4(-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{11}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245703 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245704 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1041 "field-1" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245704 13194139533671 true] [17592186245702 1110 #uuid "c391a1e2-4765-5821-997f-8890f733fbdd" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245703 1034 "\\frac{4}{11}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245703 1111 #uuid "6cecb1c6-3a1b-5e2f-a84b-92cc6c13b85d" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245704 1034 "-\\frac{4}{11}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245704 1111 #uuid "f51a9b49-6cac-5136-93b7-a9e6cef0db65" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245706 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1089 "q-341691" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1100 "Given that $y={log}_{6}⁡(-3{x}^{3}),$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ in terms of $x.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1113 #uuid "9016a16d-888e-5ccf-8278-30b6de2dd539" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1138 false 13194139533671 true] [17592186245705 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{6}⁡(u),\\,u=-3{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(6)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-9{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{uln⁡(6)}\\cdot (-9{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-9{x}^{2}}{-3{x}^{3}ln⁡(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot 3}{\\cancel{-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot xln⁡(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{xln⁡(6)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245707 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186245708 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1041 "field-1" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1104 #edb/ref 17592186245707 13194139533671 true] [17592186245706 1110 #uuid "bf1029b5-4090-506c-9b0b-049fd97904d5" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245707 1034 "\\frac{3}{x\\ln(6)}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245707 1111 #uuid "4dafbfec-c1a7-5ce8-84d6-4984fb3f1394" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245708 1034 "\\frac{1}{x\\ln(6)}" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533671 true] [17592186245708 1111 #uuid "7146ea97-87ff-56d7-94f0-6daf91862074" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186245710 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1089 "q-48559" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1100 "Given that $y={log}_{2}⁡({x}^{3}),$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1113 #uuid "d872aca0-9860-5508-b389-44ecee8a1a35" 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1138 false 13194139533671 true] [17592186245709 1145 "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={log}_{2}⁡(u),\\,u={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{uln⁡(2)},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\fra